WEBVTT

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:05.210
We're going to be working over half
of the stitches on the needle bed.

00:00:05.243 --> 00:00:08.970
Start by determining which needle is going
to be used as the center,

00:00:09.003 --> 00:00:11.810
and mark the needle bed with a pencil.

00:00:11.843 --> 00:00:15.720
This mark can be easily erased and will
help you keep track as you're transferring

00:00:15.753 --> 00:00:18.440
stitches, especially if you're
transferring groups

00:00:18.473 --> 00:00:21.290
of stitches across the row.

00:00:21.323 --> 00:00:24.520
You'll see in a minute that I didn't
remember this trick until I

00:00:24.553 --> 00:00:27.210
knit my second set of transfers.

00:00:27.243 --> 00:00:33.410
Cast on stitches as instructed and make
the first decrease, emptying a needle.

00:00:33.443 --> 00:00:38.450
Then hang a transfer tool on those first
couple of left-hand needles for safety

00:00:38.483 --> 00:00:42.120
so they won't fall off in the next step.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:49.560
Pull out all of the needles on the right
Slip those stitches to the garter bar,

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:57.530
and try to open the latches
as you remove the stitches.

00:00:57.563 --> 00:00:58.880
This isn't critical.

00:00:58.913 --> 00:01:04.520
You can always open latches, but it
helps if you do it with the garter bar.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:07.450
Transfer the stitches left.

00:01:07.483 --> 00:01:10.560
When you rehang the stitches
from the garter bar,

00:01:10.593 --> 00:01:14.200
you'll be filling in that empty needle,
and you'll have one last stitch

00:01:14.233 --> 00:01:18.560
on the right finishing your decrease.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.040
Don't forget to remove that safety

00:01:28.073 --> 00:01:33.160
transfer tool. Take that emptied needle out

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:39.880
of work before you continue knitting,
and knit two rows.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:46.410
Repeat this process,
making sure you work your decreases

00:01:46.443 --> 00:01:50.480
over the same needle each time.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:11.450
Done correctly, you'll have shaped your
piece with the decreases

00:03:11.483 --> 00:03:13.240
and have a decorative seam.

